# Story 10.8 live-validation artifacts.
#
# What is committed: everything that re-derives or adjudicates a number — the drivers
# (`measure_fallbacks.py`, `make_adjudication_sheet.py`), the pre-registration
# (`README.md`), the raw measurement ledger (`measurements.jsonl`), the adjudication
# sheets (`before_after.jpg`, `grid_<card_key>.jpg`) and the numbers behind them
# (`angle_histogram.txt`/`.json`, `adjudication_placements.json`). A reader can check
# every claim in the spec's `## Auto Run Result` from this directory alone, without a
# GPU and without re-running the pipeline.
#
# What is ignored: rendered frames and clips. THE RENDER STILL DOES NOT EXIST — the
# before/after *video* frames (story AC9) are blocked on ComfyUI and on Jay watching
# them. The images that DO exist (2026-08-16) are card-resolution sheets: the actual
# card PNG each of the 40 placements resolves to, before and after, which is an input to
# that verdict and not a substitute for it. The split:
#
#   - commit the adjudication images the verdict cites. ~512 px on the long edge is the
#     rule for a handful of frames; the contact sheets deliberately use 168–232 px cells
#     because 80 cells at 512 px is a sheet nobody scrolls, and each thumb is cropped to
#     its alpha bbox so facing stays readable (reasoned in README § Adjudication
#     artifact). Name them `before_after.*`, `*_pair.*` or `grid_*.*`: those three are
#     what the rules below un-ignore, in any image format;
#   - ignore the raw per-shot renders and full videos they were built from, which are
#     regenerable from the committed drivers against the same run. The DB snapshot
#     `make_adjudication_sheet.py` freezes is written to the system tempdir, not here,
#     so no rule is needed for it.
#
# An image dropped here under any OTHER name is ignored and will vanish silently. That
# is the trap this header exists to name — check with `git add --dry-run <path>`, not
# with `git check-ignore`, which exits 0 on a negation match too and so reads the same
# for "ignored" and "explicitly un-ignored".
#
# `git status --porcelain` on this directory proves nothing (it is ignored by design).
# Assert file state with `find _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/10-8-live-validation
# -type f` plus dates. Never blanket-delete an ignored payload here: video.py unlinks
# shot clips on re-render, so a rendered leg can be the only surviving copy.

# Ignore the raw payload by extension, then un-ignore the adjudication sheets by NAME.
# The names, not the format: the sibling 10-1b rules negated `*_pair.jpg` / `grid_*.jpg`
# against a `*.png` ignore, so every negation there was a no-op and nothing said the
# sheets had to be JPEG. Copied here, they would have silently swallowed the
# `before_after.png` this story's follow-up is specified to drop in — in a directory
# whose own header warns that `git status` proves nothing.
*.mp4
*.png
*.jpg

!before_after.*
!*_pair.*
!grid_*.*
# 2026-08-16, second session: the live-library adjudication images. They are the
# evidence that an angle LABEL is not always a facing CHANGE — a `back` card that
# draws a front-facing figure is the defect the fallback numbers cannot see — plus
# the rejected STOCK-d-class sitting set and the SCP-049 sitting control that proves
# the generation path itself works. Named explicitly rather than by prefix so the
# next writer has to think about whether their file is evidence or a raw render.
!angle_reality_grid.*
!dclass_sitting_rejected.*
!scp049_sitting_control.*
